    "summary": "NYE ’82 Oakland blaze: firey Garcia, Etta James & Tower of Power ignite a wild third set",
    "review": "The December 31, 1982 show at the Oakland Auditorium Arena captures the Dead at a festive peak. The first two sets roll strong with classics like “Cold Rain And Snow,” a seamless Sugar Magnolia→Sugaree segue, and a soaring Space → Not Fade Away jam that showcases Jerry’s blistering lead work and Brent’s tasteful keys. But the real fireworks come in the third set – a monster Turn On Your Lovelight stretched out with guest star Etta James and the thunderous Tower of Power horn section, followed by blues‑heavy “Hard To Handle” and “In The Midnight Hour.”  Across the recordings Jerry is described as “on fire,” the horns soar, and the band rides a high‑energy wave that feels perfectly timed for a New Year’s Eve celebration. While one soundboard source notes a slightly loose feel in the third set, the overall vibe remains exuberant, making this a standout entry in the early‑’80s catalog.",
